[{"id":"CON-1","class":"contract","severity":"blocking","file":"src/domain/customers.js","line":17,"what_breaks":"The email check is stricter than R-02. An email whose part after the @ starts or ends with a dot (for example 'a@.com' or 'a@b.com.') has one @, text on both sides and a dot after the @, yet it is refused with 'Enter an email like name@example.com'. No test pins this extra rule.","requirement":"R-02","evidence":"Code: `return local.length > 0 && domain.length > 0 && domain.includes('.') && !domain.startsWith('.') && !domain.endsWith('.');`. R-02: 'An email, when given, must contain one `@` with text on both sides and a dot in the part after it'. PLAN S2 Risks: 'the email rule is exactly the one in R-02 and nothing stricter.'","proven":true},{"id":"CON-2","class":"contract","severity":"advisory","file":"src/ui/customers-view.js","line":102,"what_breaks":"PLAN S7 step 4 is not done. The customer view lists the customer's orders as plain text (`el('td', `#${order.number}`)`), and app.js wires nothing to open an order from there. A user who opens a customer cannot reach any of their orders from that screen.","requirement":"R-04","evidence":"PLAN S7 step 4: '`app.js` wires the Orders tab and opening an order from the customer view.' src/ui/app.js holds only tab switching (lines 65-71). customers-view.js buildCustomerOrders has no button or handler on the rows. customers-view.js is not on S7's Files line, so S7 could not add one there.","proven":true},{"id":"CON-3","class":"contract","severity":"advisory","file":"src/ui/customers-view.js","line":95,"what_breaks":"The empty state for a customer with no orders gives no next action, although one exists: create an order for this customer. The order form also cannot be opened with this customer already chosen.","requirement":"R-20","evidence":"Code: `el('p', 'This customer has no orders yet.', { class: 'empty' })`. R-20: '... each show a short message saying so, with the next action where there is one.' Whether R-20 counts 'a customer's order list' as one of its listed states (no customers, no orders, no lines, no search results) can be read two ways.","proven":false},{"id":"CON-4","class":"contract","severity":"advisory","file":"src/ui/app.js","line":14,"what_breaks":"The UI repeats the data model's empty state, which is already defined in src/storage/store.js emptyState(). When the load fails, the views render this object, so the customer list says 'No customers yet. Use \"Add customer\"...' while data that cannot be read is still stored.","requirement":"R-18","evidence":"app.js: `const emptyState = { version: 1, nextOrderNumber: 1, customers: [], orders: [] };` and `get state() { return store.current() ?? emptyState; }`. AGENTS.md: '`src/ui/` DOM rendering and events. No business rules here.' R-18 asks only that an error is shown and the data is not overwritten. Whether a 'no customers' message under the banner counts as wrong behaviour is a judgement call.","proven":false},{"id":"CON-5","class":"contract","severity":"advisory","file":"src/ui/lines-view.js","line":20,"what_breaks":"centsToInput converts cents to a euro text in the UI. The money rule for this conversion belongs in src/domain/money.js.","requirement":"R-12","evidence":"lines-view.js: `return `${Math.floor(cents / 100)}.${String(cents % 100).padStart(2, '0')}`;`. PLAN shared design: 'Money is integer cents everywhere. Text becomes cents only in `src/domain/money.js`.' AGENTS.md: 'src/ui/ ... No business rules here.' This converts cents to text, not text to cents, so whether the plan line covers it is open.","proven":false},{"id":"CON-6","class":"contract","severity":"advisory","file":"src/ui/lines-view.js","line":7,"what_breaks":"The general DOM helpers `el` and `button` are exported from lines-view.js and imported by orders-view.js, while customers-view.js keeps its own copy. Shared helpers end up in an unrelated view module.","requirement":"none","evidence":"orders-view.js: `import { el, button, renderLines } from './lines-view.js';`. customers-view.js lines 9-20 define the same el and button again. AGENTS.md rule 7: 'Small functions, plain names, no speculative abstractions or \"utils\" dumping grounds.'","proven":false},{"id":"CON-7","class":"contract","severity":"advisory","file":"src/ui/app.js","line":5,"what_breaks":"A UI module references localStorage directly to inject it into the store.","requirement":"R-17","evidence":"app.js: `const store = createStore(window.localStorage);`. AGENTS.md: '`src/storage/` the only code that touches localStorage.' The PLAN shared design asks for injection: 'The store in `src/storage/` gets the storage object injected (`createStore(storage)`)'. Whether passing the reference counts as touching localStorage is for the human to decide.","proven":false},{"id":"CON-8","class":"contract","severity":"advisory","file":"docs/MANUAL-CHECKS.md","line":5,"what_breaks":"Commit b00627a ticks all 23 manual checks at once under the message 'Manual checks', which is not in the `S<n>: ... (R-xx)` form. Nothing in the repository shows which checks a human actually ran.","requirement":"none","evidence":"git log: 'b00627a Bita Ioan | Manual checks', and that diff changes every line from '- [ ]' to '- [x]'. AGENTS.md rule 8: 'One commit per finished slice: `S<n>: <what changed> (R-xx, R-yy)`.' ADR-002: 'The human ... ticks only the manual checks they ran'. Authorship alone cannot settle whether a human or an agent ran them.","proven":false},{"id":"CON-9","class":"contract","severity":"advisory","file":".github/workflows/gate.yml","line":1,"what_breaks":"Commit 6ac3155 adds the new folders .github/workflows/ and .githooks/, which are not in the AGENTS.md structure and not on any plan slice.","requirement":"none","evidence":"AGENTS.md rule 5: 'No new dependencies and no folders outside the structure above.' ADR-001 'Not decided here: Configuration files at the repository root'. ADR-002 does cover them: 'One gate script ... runs in the Claude hooks, in the git hooks and in CI.' So these may be human-decided kit files rather than slice output.","proven":false}]
